T224 - LoginHandlers.OnGetUserList: send the three S_GET_USER_LIST delete fields from
ServerConfig.xml instead of the hardcoded 5 / 0 / 72.

Handlers/LoginHandlers.cs is human-owned, so this is the diff rather than an edit. It is the
ONLY change T224 needs in that file: the per-character isDeleting / deleteTime /
deleteRemainSec are already overwritten by CharacterHandlers.FillLobbyFields, which this
handler calls per element (T122's arrangement, unchanged).

Why it matters: this deployment's <DeleteUser expireHour1="0" expireHour2="72"
deletionSectionClassifyLevel="5" /> happens to equal the hardcoded values, so the three fields
looked right. Set expireHour2="0" - as the T224 repro did - and the client is still told the
window is 72 h while the server now deletes immediately, so character select shows a countdown
for a character that is already gone.

Pinned: cap_final_client2 frame 11, S_GET_USER_LIST fixed part at frame offset 8 reads
veteran 0, bonusBufSec 0, maxCharacters 3, first 1, more 0, leftDelTimeAccountOver 0,
deletionSectionClassifyLevel 5, deleteCharacterExpireHour1 0, deleteCharacterExpireHour2 72 -
i.e. retail sends the file's own three numbers, and 259200 s (72 h) is exactly the
deleteRemainSec the same frame carries for the character being deleted.

--- a/src/TeraSharp.Arbiter/Handlers/LoginHandlers.cs
+++ b/src/TeraSharp.Arbiter/Handlers/LoginHandlers.cs
@@
+        // T224: ServerConfig.xml <DeleteUser> owns these three, not this file. CharacterDeletion
+        // reads it once and caches; CharacterDeletion.UseForTests overrides it in the harness.
+        var delPolicy = Persistence.CharacterDeletion.Current;
+
         s.SendByDef("S_GET_USER_LIST", new Dictionary<string, object>
         {
             ["characters"] = characters, ["veteran"] = false, ["bonusBufSec"] = 0, ["maxCharacters"] = QaUtilityCommands.CharacterSlots(Program.Store, (long)s.Account.AccountId),
             ["first"] = true, ["more"] = false, ["leftDelTimeAccountOver"] = 0,
-            ["deletionSectionClassifyLevel"] = 5, ["deleteCharacterExpireHour1"] = 0, ["deleteCharacterExpireHour2"] = 72,
+            ["deletionSectionClassifyLevel"] = delPolicy.ClassifyLevel,
+            ["deleteCharacterExpireHour1"] = delPolicy.ExpireHour1,
+            ["deleteCharacterExpireHour2"] = delPolicy.ExpireHour2,
         });
